  "description": "Partition 4D image feature tensor (B, H, W, C) into non-overlapping spatial windows of size (M, M) and reverse back to original layout.\n\nBy confining self-attention within local M x M windows, Swin Transformer reduces attention complexity from quadratic O((HW)^2) to linear O(M^2 HW).\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\n\\mathbf{X}_{\\text{windows}} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{\\left(B \\frac{H}{M} \\frac{W}{M}\\right) \\times M \\times M \\times C}\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Reshape 4D tensor into 6D grid tensor (B, H/M, M, W/M, M, C)\n2. Permute axes to group window tokens contiguous in memory (B * num_windows, M, M, C)\n3. Verify invertible reconstruction back to original (B, H, W, C) dimensions\n\n### Returns\nDictionary with 'num_windows', 'window_shape', and boolean 'is_reconstructible'.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Window Partition and Reverse\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nImages have unique spatial properties: neighboring pixels are strongly correlated, and visual patterns (like edges, corners, or textures) appear anywhere in an image. Computer vision algorithms use spatial inductive biases like translation equivariance and local receptive fields to process image grids efficiently. **Window Partition and Reverse** operates directly on spatial coordinates or bounding box geometries.\n\nBy confining self-attention within local M x M windows, Swin Transformer reduces attention complexity from quadratic O((HW)^2) to linear O(M^2 HW). In this problem, the goal is to: partition 4d image feature tensor (b, h, w, c) into non-overlapping spatial windows of size (m, m) and reverse back to original layout.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{X}_{\\text{windows}} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{\\left(B \\frac{H}{M} \\frac{W}{M}\\right) \\times M \\times M \\times C}\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Reshape 4D tensor into 6D grid tensor (B, H/M, M, W/M, M, C)\n2. **Phase 2**: Permute axes to group window tokens contiguous in memory (B * num_windows, M, M, C)\n3. **Phase 3**: Verify invertible reconstruction back to original (B, H, W, C) dimensions\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Spatial Locality**: Sliding spatial filters across multi-channel feature maps aggregates contextual clues across local neighborhoods.\n* **Object Detection Pipelines**: Bounding box metrics (such as IoU and Non-Maximum Suppression) reconcile duplicate candidate detections into clean, final predictions.\n* **Data Augmentation**: Geometric transformations expose models to diverse spatial viewpoints, significantly improving generalization to unseen test images.",
